---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import fs from 'node:fs';
import path from 'node:path';

const hasPhoto = fs.existsSync(path.join(process.cwd(), 'public/images/tee.jpg'));
---

<Layout
  title="About"
  description="The Product Bet is a blog about tech product management, voice AI products, and moving from engineering into product."
  narrow
>
  <header class="hero">
    <p class="eyebrow">About</p>
    <h1>Hi, I'm Tee</h1>
  </header>
  <article class="prose">
    {hasPhoto && <img src="/images/tee.jpg" alt="Tee" width="160" height="160" class="about-photo" />}

    <p>
      I'm a product manager. I've worked on B2B SaaS, voice AI agents, and enterprise mobile
      products, and I came into product from an engineering background.
    </p>
    <p>
      The Product Bet is where I write about what I'm learning on the job: shipping voice AI
      products, the engineer-to-PM transition, and the everyday craft of product management. Most
      posts are things I wish someone had told me a year earlier.
    </p>
    <p>I publish one post a week. If that sounds useful, subscribe below and it'll land in your inbox.</p>

    <h2>What I write about</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Voice AI products — what actually breaks, and which metrics matter</li>
      <li>Engineer to PM — what transfers, what doesn't, and how to make the move</li>
      <li>Building in public — build logs from my side projects</li>
      <li>PM craft — PRDs, prioritisation, and interviews</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Elsewhere</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><a href="https://tabassumkhanum.in" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Portfolio</a></li>
      <li><a href="https://linkedin.com/in/tabassum-khanum" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">LinkedIn</a></li>
      <li><a href="https://github.com/tabassum2507" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">GitHub</a></li>
    </ul>
  </article>
</Layout>
